      "eyebrow": "Quick answer",
      "heading": "Quick answer",
      "html": "<p>A fleet vehicle inspection has two parts: the driver's walkaround check before the vehicle is used, and the mechanic's planned safety inspection at set intervals. For cars, light vans and light trailers the legal minimum tyre tread is 1.6 mm across the central three-quarters of the tread and around the whole circumference. For goods and passenger vehicles under an operator licence, DVSA's guide expects at least one walkaround check in every 24-hour period the vehicle is in service, safety inspections normally every 4 to 13 weeks, and records kept for at least 15 months.</p><p>Sources: The Highway Code, Annex 6 (gov.uk); DVSA, Guide to maintaining roadworthiness: commercial goods and passenger carrying vehicles (gov.uk, updated 28 April 2025). Checked on 18 November 2026.</p>"
    },
    {
