      "heading": "What to do when you find a defect",
      "html": "<p>Finding a defect means the system works.</p><p>Record it at once. Note the registration, date, time, the defect and the driver. Add a photo.</p><p>Tell the fleet manager before the van moves. Is it safe to use? The driver and operator decide. A bulge in a tyre means the van does not move.</p><p>Record the repair too. A defect with no repair record is a gap: the DVSA guide expects reports to record faults and the rectification work. See the <a href=\"/pages/van-defect-report-uk.html\">van defect report template</a>.</p>"
    },
