      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>What is the difference between a walkaround and planned maintenance?</h3><p>The walkaround is the driver's check before each journey. Lights, tyres, fluids, body and load. Planned maintenance is the mechanic's job at set times. It covers what the driver cannot see.</p><h3>Who does the daily walkaround?</h3><p>The driver. Under the DVSA guide, drivers must report defects to a responsible person with the authority to act.</p><h3>What is the legal tyre tread minimum for light vans?</h3><p>1.6mm across the middle three-quarters of the tread, all the way round. Many fleets act at 3mm.</p><h3>Must the checklist be signed?</h3><p>The DVSA guide has the driver sign to confirm they understand their responsibilities in writing, and says drivers' defect reports must be kept for at least 15 months. I did not find a signature on every daily check required. Keep the record showing who did the check, and when. See the <a href=\"/pages/van-check-app-uk.html\">van check app for UK fleets</a> and the <a href=\"/pages/dvsa-walkaround-check-free-template-uk.html\">DVSA walkaround check free template</a>.</p>"
